! Ideal silicon at a production cutoff, for an equation of state.
!
! The two-atom LDA cell of `si2-nc-stress.in` with the displaced atom put back on
! its ideal site and the cutoff raised from 12 Ry to 40. Both changes are what an
! E(V) curve needs and neither is what a stress reference needs, which is why
! this is a separate input rather than a variant of that one.
!
! The atom is on its site so that the curve is an equation of state and not a
! mixture of one with a displaced atom relaxing as the cell is scaled.
!
! The cutoff is the point of the file. Expanding the cell at a fixed `ecutwfc`
! lets more plane waves inside the sphere, so the basis improves as the volume
! grows and the energy falls for a reason that is not physics -- the Pulay
! stress. On this cell it is about 44 kbar at 12 Ry, 1.1 kbar at 40 and 0.11 at
! 60, so 40 is where `tr sigma / 3` and `-dE/dV` can be plotted on one axis and
! seen to agree.
!
! There is no committed `pw.x` reference beside this one and none is needed: what
! it is for is the agreement of two derivatives computed here, one taken at a
! single volume with the wavefunctions frozen and one differenced across
! separately converged runs.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    tstress = .true.
 /
 &system
    ibrav=2, celldm(1)=10.20, nat=2, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=40.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 4 4 4 0 0 0
